  },
  {
   "text": "Unreal, default exe name",
   "start": 12.851,
   "duration": 11.583,
   "x": 560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Python 3.11 in the build",
   "start": 13.301,
   "duration": 11.133,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "DirectML + ONNX",
   "start": 13.751,
   "duration": 10.683,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "This horror demo shipped with Python\ninside it. And a machine learning runtime.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 4.904
  },
  {
   "text": "In a game about noticing\nwhen something has changed.",
   "start": 5.154,
   "duration": 2.997
  },
  {
   "text": "Let's do the game first, because\nthis one is worth explaining.",
   "start": 12.001,
   "duration": 3.415
  },
  {
   "text": "COMPARTMENT 666 is an anomaly hunt. You wake up on a train with no memory\nof boarding it, and the only way forward is through the carriages.",
   "start": 15.666,
   "duration": 8.718
  },
  {
   "text": "You walk into a compartment. You look at it. Then you\ndecide one thing: is this normal, or has something changed.",
   "start": 24.634,
   "duration": 7.281
  },
  {
   "text": "Say normal when it's normal, and the train moves on. Say\nit wrong, either way, and you lose a life. You get three.",
   "start": 32.165,
   "duration": 7.595
  },
  {
   "text": "If you've played Exit 8, you know the shape of this. It's the loop that game\nturned into a genre: same room, again and again, and the only skill is noticing.",
   "start": 40.01,
   "duration": 9.606
  },
  {
   "text": "What this one adds is a radio. A little handheld device that picks\nup anomalies you can't see, and you don't get to use it forever.",
   "start": 49.866,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "The dressing is an early 1900s express. Red velvet, oil paintings, brass. Which is a\nsmart choice, because a period carriage is full of objects you don't have a memory for.",
   "start": 63.946,
   "duration": 10.442
  },
  {
   "text": "And the anomalies are graded easy, medium and hard, with a\ndifferent death animation waiting when you get one wrong.",
   "start": 74.638,
   "duration": 6.576
  },
  {
   "text": "It went up on Steam today. Single player, fifteen languages, no reviews\nyet. Which means the only thing I can actually check is the build.",
   "start": 81.464,
   "duration": 8.065
  },
  {
   "text": "So. One point four eight\ngigabytes, thirty six files.",
   "start": 89.779,
   "duration": 4.382
  },
  {
   "text": "Unreal Engine, and almost all of it is one container:\none point one six gigabytes in a single ucas.",
   "start": 94.411,
   "duration": 7.308
  },
  {
   "text": "Then I looked at the executable, and\nit isn't called what you'd expect.",
   "start": 101.969,
   "duration": 4.121
  },
  {
   "text": "The launcher is COMPARTMENT_666 dot exe. But the actual binary, the\nhundred and forty megabyte one, is called UnrealGame-Win64-Shipping.",
   "start": 106.34,
   "duration": 10.521
  },
  {
   "text": "That's Unreal's default. Every other Unreal demo\nI've opened renamed it. This project never did.",
   "start": 117.111,
   "duration": 5.923
  },
  {
   "text": "Once you've seen that, the rest\nof the list reads a certain way.",
   "start": 123.284,
   "duration": 3.886
  },
  {
   "text": "d3d12SDKLayers.dll. Five and a half megabytes. That's the DirectX\n12 debug layer, and it exists to help a developer find bugs.",
   "start": 127.42,
   "duration": 10.703
  },
  {
   "text": "Three episodes ago Square Enix shipped that exact file.\nSame file, same reason: nobody tightened the shipping config.",
   "start": 138.373,
   "duration": 7.36
  },
  {
   "text": "Then nine Boost libraries. And one of\nthem is boost python three eleven.",
   "start": 145.983,
   "duration": 4.617
  },
  {
   "text": "Unreal has a Python plugin. It's for the editor: build scripts,\nasset pipelines, tools. It has no job in the copy a player downloads.",
   "start": 150.85,
   "duration": 8.483
  },
  {
   "text": "It's here because the plugin was\nnever switched off before packaging.",
   "start": 159.583,
   "duration": 3.52
  },
  {
   "text": "And then the two that made me stop. DirectML,\nthirteen megabytes. ONNX Runtime, thirteen more.",
   "start": 163.353,
   "duration": 7.099
  },
  {
   "text": "That's a machine learning inference stack, in a game whose\nwhole mechanic is spotting a difference between two rooms.",
   "start": 170.702,
   "duration": 6.158
  },
  {
   "text": "I want that to be something. It probably isn't. Unreal's neural network plugin drags both\nin, and this is the second demo I've opened where they're present with nothing to point at.",
   "start": 177.11,
   "duration": 10.233
  },
  {
   "text": "If you made this and I'm wrong,\nthe comments are right there.",
   "start": 187.593,
   "duration": 3.128
  },
  {
   "text": "One more. Seventeen megabytes of Epic Online Services,\nin a game the store lists as single player only.",
   "start": 190.971,
   "duration": 7.046
  },
  {
   "text": "Achievements, telemetry, a plan for\nlater. A file list can't say which.",
   "start": 198.267,
   "duration": 5.139
  },
  {
   "text": "Reception. There isn't any. It went up this morning,\nno reviews, no player numbers worth reading.",
   "start": 203.656,
   "duration": 6.263
  },
  {
   "text": "So here's the honest read instead. The idea is proven, the train is a good room to hide\nthings in, and this build is a first pass that shipped exactly as it left the editor.",
   "start": 210.169,
   "duration": 9.737
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 220.156,
   "duration": 2.397
  },
  {
   "text": "Unreal, thirty six files, the default executable\nname, a debug layer, Python, and an ML runtime.",
   "start": 222.803,
   "duration": 6.524
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip. It's free, it's a genre that works, and finding\nthe anomaly in a red velvet carriage is a good twenty minutes.",
   "start": 229.577,
   "duration": 7.308
  },
  {
   "text": "If you ship in Unreal, take the packaging list from this one. Rename the target, turn\noff the Python plugin, and check for SDKLayers. Three checkboxes, ninety megabytes.",
   "start": 237.135,
   "duration": 10.651
  },
  {
   "text": "That's my read from the outside. If you worked on this and I got something wrong, say so\nand I'll pin the correction. Next time, another demo, another file list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 248.036,
   "duration": 9.868
  }
 ],
